The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
P->screen_max = 0.0;
double m = simint_primscreen(A, B, P->screen + idx, screen_method);
P->screen_max = (m > P->screen_max ? m : P->screen_max);
```
Reason:
Initializing `P->screen_max` to zero means that any computed screening value `m` that is less than or equal to zero will not update `screen_max`, potentially leading to incorrect behavior in subsequent calculations that rely on `screen_max` being a meaningful positive value.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
P->screen_max = 1.e99;
double m = simint_primscreen(A, B, P->screen + idx, screen_method);
P->screen_max = (m > P->screen_max ? m : P->screen_max);
```
Reason:
By initializing `P->screen_max` to a very large value (`1.e99`), any valid computed screening value `m` will be able to update `screen_max`, ensuring that it reflects the maximum screening value encountered during the calculations, thus correcting the behavior of the function.

